{"step_index":5148,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T07:58:10Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-25T07:58:10Z\nCompleted At: 2026-09-25T07:58:10Z\nFile Path: `file:///home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/AGENTS.md`\nTotal Lines: 314\nTotal Bytes: 17890\nShowing lines 70 to 140\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n70: - **Request Classification:** Automatically classifies incoming requests into 8 distinct categories:\n71:   1. `general question`\n72:   2. `research`\n73:   3. `project work`\n74:   4. `multi-project work`\n75:   5. `monitoring`\n76:   6. `incident`\n77:   7. `corrective action`\n78:   8. `architecture decision`\n79: - **Authority:** Full orchestrator authority. Evaluates and approves Level 2B actions. Coordinates human confirmation for Level 3. Performs final acceptance of completed tasks.\n80: \n81: ### 2.2 ASKING & RESEARCH AGENT\n82: - **Identifier:** `agy:ask`\n83: - **Role:** Technical Researcher & General Question Assistant\n84: - **Workspace:** `/home/azureuser/Ask-And-Research`\n85: - **Boundary:** Global READ ONLY across all server projects and documentation.\n86: - **WhatsApp Behavior:** Connects directly to WhatsApp to answer general and technical inquiries (e.g., modern AI architectures, Rust diagnostics, Azure architecture).\n87: - **Hard Restriction:** Strict READ ONLY. Cannot modify production code, delete files, restart critical services, or execute destructive actions.\n88: \n89: ### 2.3 REPORTING AGENT (GLOBAL SENTINEL)\n90: - **Identifier:** `agy:report`\n91: - **Role:** Global Observability, Watchdog & Independent System Health Sentinel\n92: - **Workspace:** `/home/azureuser/Reporting-Agent`\n93: - **Boundary:** Global READ/AUDIT ONLY across all projects, process states, and logs.\n94: - **Primary Job:** Continuous observation to detect failures across 20+ classes:\n95:   - Agent stopped / crashed / stalled / stuck in loop\n96:   - Task claimed completed without tangible evidence\n97:   - Build failure / test failure / syntax error / runtime crash\n98:   - Project boundary violations / unauthorized access\n99:   - Abnormal resource consumption (CPU/RAM spikes)\n100:   - WhatsApp bridge / daemon failure\n101: - **Zero Direct Fix Mandate:** The Reporting Agent **NEVER modifies production code directly**. Detecting an issue triggers a structured `INCIDENT` JSON written to `/home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/INCIDENTS/active/`.\n102: - **Decoupled Verification Role:** Does NOT grade or validate the Action Agent's patch logic directly. Instead, it performs **Independent System Health Monitoring** to confirm whether the service remains healthy and error-free after deployment.\n103: \n104: ### 2.4 ACTION AGENT (CONTROLLED FIXER)\n105: - **Identifier:** `agy:action`\n106: - **Role:** Incident Response, Containment & Corrective Action Engine\n107: - **Workspace:** `/home/azureuser/Action-Agent`\n108: - **Boundary:** Controlled Cross-Project Write Authority strictly subject to Safety Levels (0 to 3) enforced by the Policy/Tool Gateway.\n109: - **Anti-Blindness Protocol:** Before applying any fix, the Action Agent must independently verify the incident evidence.\n110: - **Execution Rules:**\n111:   1. Inspect existing state and git status.\n112:   2. Plan isolated, minimal corrective action.\n113:   3. Classify action by Safety Level (0, 1, 2A, 2B, 3).\n114:   4. If Level 2B, request Master Agent approval token.\n115:   5. If Level 3, request Iraq Bhai WhatsApp confirmation.\n116:   6. Run automated tests / syntax checks before and after modification.\n117:   7. Record git diff and test output.\n118: \n119: ### 2.5 DOMAIN-LOCKED PROJECT AGENTS (WORKERS)\n120: - **YouTube Pipeline:** `/home/azureuser/.openclaw/workspace/IROSCRIPT-CEO/social-media/youtube` (Veo 3.1 Chrome Extension only, SQLite single source of truth).\n121: - **Frappe & ERPNext:** `/home/azureuser/Frappe-erp-Alco` (ERPNext v16, mobile-first frontend).\n122: - **Telegram Bot:** `/home/azureuser/telegram-bot` (Live MTProto/Telethon search only, no local JSON/CSV fallback).\n123: - **Digital History:** `/home/azureuser/.openclaw/workspace/IROSCRIPT-CEO/PERSONAL AI AGENT` (Protected OpenRecall daemon).\n124: - **Kids Tube:** `/home/azureuser/kids_tube_with_folder_seection`.\n125: - **Rust Task:** `/home/azureuser/Rust_Task_With_Time_Keeping_And_Live_Note` (Cargo build verification).\n126: - **Article Publishing:** `/home/azureuser/Article-Publishing-Platform`.\n127: - **3D / Game Studio:** `/home/azureuser/3D-Game-Design-Studio`.\n128: - **Zero Cross-Project Access:** Each project agent is strictly restricted to its own workspace. Cross-project file reads, writes, executions, or directory traversals are intercepted and denied by the boundary guard.\n129: \n130: ---\n131: \n132: ## 3. ACTION SAFETY LEVELS & APPROVAL MATRIX\n133: \n134: To ensure that the Action Agent's cross-project write capability can never cause unintended side-effects across the server, write permissions are stratified:\n135: \n136: | Level | Name | Scope & Allowed Operations | Required Approval |\n137: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n138: | **0** | **READ_ONLY** | Safe read, inspect, audit, diagnostic runs, web research. | **None** |\n139: | **1** | **LOW_IMPACT_REVERSIBLE** | Cache cleanup, temporary diagnostic scripts, safe service restarts. | **Policy Gate Check** |\n140: | **2A** | **ISOLATED_TESTED_PATCH** | Small, isolated bug fix inside a single file with unit tests passing. | **Automated Policy Gate (No human block if tests pass)** |\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
